      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "Given that $r(t)=⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩,$ $|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})|=$",
      "worked_solution": "Evaluating the function at $t=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3}),\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{3})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing the magnitude of this vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|r(\\frac{\\pi }{3})| & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
